<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady, meal firm, oil better.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady, meal firm, oil better.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices remained steady in central Indian markets in very thin trading on Thursday, dealers said.</p>
<p>Arrivals were around 1,000 tonnes, compared to 15,000 tonnes per day at the same time last year. The undertone was firm.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were slightly better on good demand in local market. Business volumes were dull and the undertone steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were firm on good export demand against poor offtake. Soymeal yellow was $303-304 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $115 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was 3,950-3,975 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business volume was limited and the undertone was strong.</p>
